  Here’s a bit of code in ]8;id=3954320270;https://haskell.org[1mHaskell[m]8;; [38;5;99;4m]8;id=3954320270;https://haskell.orghttps://haskell.org]8;;[m, because we are fancy.  
  Remember that to compile Haskell you’ll need [38;5;212;48;5;236m ghc [m.                         
                                                                              
  module Main where                                                           
                                                                              
  import Data.List (intercalate)                                              
                                                                              
  hello :: String -> String                                                   
  hello s = "Hello, " <> s <> "."                                             
                                                                              
  main :: IO ()                                                               
  main = putStrLn                                                             
       $ intercalate "\n"                                                     
       $ hello <$> [ "artichoke", "alcachofa" ]                               
  [38;5;212m[m                                                                            
  [38;5;212m──────[m                                                                      
  [38;5;212m[m                                                                            
  [3mAlcachofa[m, if you were wondering, is artichoke in Spanish.                  
